1
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:06,070
为什么这年代了召唤蝙蝠侠还用蝙蝠信号灯
But why do they still call Batman using the Bat-Signal?

2
00:00:06,070 --> 00:00:08,080
直接发条短信请他来不是更方便吗
Wouldn't it just be, like, easier to text him?

3
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:10,430
蝙蝠信号灯不只是用来召唤蝙蝠侠
The Bat-Signal isn't just to alert Batman,

4
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:12,780
还有震慑他敌人内心的功用
it's also to strike fear in the hearts of his enemies

5
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:14,000
让他们知道蝙蝠侠要来了
and let them know he's coming.

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,500
就像谢尔顿的三段敲门法
Sort of like Sheldon's knock.

7
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:20,550
嘲讽我跟蝙蝠侠类似吗  我接受
Comparing me to Batman? I'll take it.

8
00:00:21,570 --> 00:00:23,020
如果我们不出手
If we don't do anything,

9
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:25,090
你们觉得他们能聊多久的蝙蝠侠
how long do you think they'll talk about Batman?

10
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:28,030
我认识他们已经有11年了  所以...
Well, I've know them for 11 years, so...

11
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:29,730
11年吧
11 years.

12
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:32,500
我觉得他们也有给他发短信
I believe they do text him.

13
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,400
蝙蝠信号灯通过蓝牙连到他手机
The-the Bat-Signal is linked to his phone via Bluetooth.

14
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,660
漫画里有画过吗
Has that been in the comics?

15
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:38,670
没  我个人这么认为而已
No, it's just what I believe.

16
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:41,500
够了  我要让他们停下
All right, I'm putting a stop to this.

17
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,210
你如果知道办法  你为什么还等了11年啊
If you knew how, why'd you wait 11 years?

18
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:46,810
各位  告诉你们
Hey, guys, guess what?

19
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:51,740
我今天上班发现我要跟比尔·盖茨见面了
Today at work, I found out I am going to meet Bill Gates.

20
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:54,950
抱歉  莱纳德  你跟佩妮的缘分到此为止了
Sorry, Leonard, you and Penny had a good run.

21
00:00:57,330 --> 00:01:00,780
你确定吗  我猜他家的网应该超快呢
You sure? I-I bet his Internet's really fast.

22
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:02,430
你怎么会有此荣幸
How did this happen?

23
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:04,310
他的慈善基金会在寻找
Well, his foundation is looking to partner

24
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,970
我不会为了比尔·盖茨而甩了他
I'm not leaving him for Bill Gates.

25
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:07,250
制药公司来合作研发价格低廉的疫苗
with a pharmaceutical company to help develop affordable vaccines

26
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:09,180
所以公司让我带他转转
so they asked me to show him around.

27
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:10,680
太好了  他什么时候来
That's great. When's he coming?

28
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:12,810
他大概周日  周一早晨到
Uh, he gets in on Sunday, and Monday morning,

29
00:01:12,810 --> 00:01:15,210
我会带他去看看实验室和办公区域
I'm gonna give him a tour of the labs and offices.

30
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:19,760
他周日  也就是4月1号到吗
Oh. He gets in on Sunday, April first?

31
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:22,020
想得美  佩妮
Nice try, Penny.

32
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,140
你在说什么
What're you talking about?

33
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:25,620
4月1日愚人节
April Fools' Day.

34
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:27,490
想必这又是另一个你年年
This is another one of your classic pranks

35
00:01:27,490 --> 00:01:29,350
想愚弄我的恶作剧之一吧
you try to pull on me every year.

36
00:01:29,350 --> 00:01:31,850
我从来没有对你恶作剧过啊
Literally never pulled a prank on you.

37
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:33,350
是吗  那去年
Oh, really? What about last year,

38
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:35,620
你给我发一封电邮写了照片请见附件
when you sent me that e-mail with the photo attached,

39
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:38,280
结果根本没附件
but you didn't attach a photo.

40
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:39,810
那是我犯错了
That was a mistake.

41
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:42,440
想耍我  你当然是犯了错
Messing with me? Yes, it was.

42
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:43,600
所以今年
And this year,

43
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,030
我不会再上你的当
I am not falling for it.

44
00:01:45,030 --> 00:01:47,610
-谢尔顿  我发誓...  -别  你这是在干嘛
- Sheldon, I swear... - No... what are you doing?

45
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:51,050
被你猜中了  他没有要来  愚人节
Oh, you're right. He's not coming. April fools.

46
00:01:51,350 --> 00:01:52,260
常言道
You know what they say,

47
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:53,970
耍我"N"次
fool me "N" Times,

48
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:56,290
"N"等于你已经耍到我的次数
where "N" equals the amount of times you've already fooled me,

49
00:01:56,290 --> 00:01:57,350
你傻逼
shame on you.

50
00:01:57,350 --> 00:02:01,170
耍我"N+1"次  我傻逼
Fool me "N" plus one times, shame on me.

51
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,570
生

52
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,570
活

53
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,570
大

54
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,570
爆

55
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,570
炸

56
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:22,570
第十一季  第十八集

57
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:32,100
所以你要跟比尔·盖茨共处一天
So you're gonna spend a day with Bill Gates.

58
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:33,360
我有点小嫉妒啊
I'm a little jealous.

59
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,730
我还有点小紧张呢
Well, I'm a little nervous.

60
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,730
如果我这次做得好  我希望公司能考虑一下
You know, if I do a good job, I'm hoping they'll consider me

61
00:02:36,730 --> 00:02:38,820
最近刚空出来的公关职位
for a PR position that's opening up.

62
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:41,540
如果你很紧张  我知道很多关于他的事
Well, if you're nervous, I-I know a lot about him.

63
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:45,450
我可以帮你补习  或者陪你一起  我都行
I can fill you in or maybe come along, whatever.

64
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:47,650
我觉得我没事的
I think I'll be okay.

65
00:02:47,650 --> 00:02:49,710
我举个例子  万一他想要
Well, I'm-I'm just saying, what are you gonna do

66
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:52,100
跟你聊微型计算机的
when he wants to talk about high-level language interpreters

67
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:53,320
高级语言翻译程序怎么办
for microcomputers?

68
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:56,510
什么是微型计算机的高级语言翻译程序啊
What are high-level language interpreters for microcomputers?

69
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:58,150
一种为电脑编程的方式
A way of programming computers

70
00:02:58,150 --> 00:03:00,490
是用语言与指令而不是用二进制代码
using words and commands instead of binary code.

71
00:03:00,490 --> 00:03:03,200
这还挺有意思的呢  再跟我说说
Oh. That's actually kind of interesting. Tell me more.

72
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:03,980
其实嘛...
Oh, well...

73
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,380
这样  我会用这招回他
That, I'll do that. Mm-hmm.

74
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:10,430
-我真是完全没料到啊  -是啊
- I didn't even see it coming. - Yeah, well...

75
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:12,400
你从来都没料到过
You never do.

76
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:15,460
只是...  只是他是我的一个偶像
Well, I-it's just, he's an idol of mine

77
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,650
我真的很想有机会跟他见见面
and I would love the chance to hang out with him.

78
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:18,730
我知道你想见他
Look, I know you want to meet him,

79
00:03:18,730 --> 00:03:20,640
但我不能把这事变成社交活动  好吗
but I can't turn this into a social thing, okay?

80
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:23,350
这是我的工作  我得确保这事办得妥当
This is my job. I really need it to go well.

81
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,790
懂  我懂  你说得对
I get it, I get it. You're right.

82
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,160
其实  其实我以前已经见过他一次了啦
Actually, I've-I've already met him once before.

83
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,310
他在普林斯顿大学演讲  我妈带我去了
He gave a talk at Princeton and my mom took me.

84
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:31,610
真的吗  他人好相处吗
Oh, really? Was he nice?

85
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:33,170
人超好
He's super nice.

86
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:36,530
后来我太激动就开始哭了什么的...
I-I got pretty emotional and started crying and...

87
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,220
他也没有取笑我什么的
He didn't make fun of me or anything.

88
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:41,540
你当时只是个孩子嘛
Well, you were a kid.

89
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:48,540
嗯哼
Uh-huh.

90
00:03:51,030 --> 00:03:53,710
再见了  孩子们  我爱你们
Bye, my babies, I love you.

91
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:56,560
妈咪  我们也爱你
We love you, too, Mommy.

92
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:58,880
下次不许再恶心我
Yeah, don't do that.

93
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,350
伯纳黛特
Bernadette?

94
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:05,360
-你们要去哪里  -公园[西语]
- Hi. Where you off to? - El parque.

95
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,890
公园[西语]吗
El parque?

96
00:04:06,890 --> 00:04:10,230
我在学西语  这样才能跟其他保姆聊天
I'm learning Spanish so I can talk to the other nannies.

97
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:12,710
学得如何
How's that going?

98
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:14,160
好[西语]
Bueno.

99
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:16,260
好啊
Good?

100
00:04:19,970 --> 00:04:21,650
不  好[西语]
No bueno.

101
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:28,420
-谢谢你来陪我  -小事
- Thanks for coming over. - No problem.

102
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:29,570
想喝什么吗
Can I get you anything?

103
00:04:29,570 --> 00:04:31,730
果汁  "蕉蕉"
Juice box? 'Naners?

104
00:04:32,090 --> 00:04:33,330
什么是"蕉蕉"
'Naners?

105
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:35,050
抱歉  当妈的脑子
Sorry. Mom brain.

106
00:04:35,050 --> 00:04:37,430
我都快忘了怎么跟成人说话了
I think I've forgot how to talk to grown-ups.

107
00:04:37,430 --> 00:04:39,930
我是说香蕉蕉
I meant ba-naners.

108
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:42,170
没事啦  不用了
You know what, I'm good.

109
00:04:42,170 --> 00:04:43,420
好吧
Okay.

110
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:45,260
我们看的这是什么
So, what are we watching?

111
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:47,450
《建筑师巴布》  我帮你补一下剧情
Bob the Builder. I'll catch you up.

112
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:49,110
这位就是巴布
That one's Bob.

113
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,480
他是个建筑师
He's a builder.

114
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:54,720
这不是儿童节目吗
Isn't this a kids show?

115
00:04:54,990 --> 00:04:57,640
我们家里就看这个
It's what we watch in this house.

116
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:59,570
《建筑师巴布》《恐龙列车》
Bob the Builder, Dinosaur Train,

117
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:03,410
《小猪佩奇》  逗趣又意义深远
and Peppa Pig, which is both funny and meaningful.

118
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:07,960
你要不要休息一下  一起去吃点东西
You want to take a break and maybe get something to eat?

119
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,220
好啊
Sure.

120
00:05:12,230 --> 00:05:14,680
怎么感觉不到有要出发的意思
Why does it not feel like we're going?

121
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:17,670
稍等  我看看巴布能不能修好
Hang on, I-I just want to see if Bob can fix it.

122
00:05:19,090 --> 00:05:21,260
巴布的招牌台词  Yes, I / we can.

123
00:05:19,090 --> 00:05:21,260
是的  他可以
Yes, he can!

124
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:26,530
你来啦
Oh, hey.

125
00:05:26,530 --> 00:05:30,150
我替你折好了衣服  不用谢
I folded your laundry for you. You're welcome.

126
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,340
那不是我的啊
Uh, that's not mine.

127
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:38,690
你的意思是  这些不是你的
You're saying that these aren't yours?

128
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,170
不是
No.

129
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:51,380
所以你的意思是  我正摸着
So you're saying that I'm touching

130
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,830
陌生人的内裤
a stranger's underpants?

131
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:55,160
是的
Yes.

132
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:06,710
就这样  今天成了我人生最惨的一天
And just like that, it's the worst day of my life.

133
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:10,640
等等  你为什么要怪里怪气的
Wait, why are you being so weird?

134
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,130
因为我想到比尔·盖茨的事有可能是真的
It occurred to me that perhaps you were telling the truth about Bill Gates

135
00:06:15,130 --> 00:06:17,730
而不是只是你精心铺垫的恶作剧一环
and it wasn't just part of an elaborate prank.

136
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,900
恶作剧的部分会是什么啊
What would the prank part even be?

137
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:23,410
我跑去见比尔·盖茨  尽管你说"不许来"
I show up to meet Bill Gates over your "objections,"

138
00:06:23,410 --> 00:06:24,950
结果到场了才发现不是比尔·盖茨
but it's not Bill Gates at all, no.

139
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:28,040
是那种你聘请来派对的名人装扮者
It's one of those look-alikes that you hire for a party.

140
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:29,080
而当我手里拿着
And then when I go around

141
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:30,530
"比尔·盖茨"给我折的气球玩具
showing everybody the balloon animal

142
00:06:30,530 --> 00:06:33,610
到处让别人看时  我就会像个智障
that "Bill Gates" made for me, I'll look like an idiot.

143
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:38,650
你是不是偷偷喝洗衣液了
Have you been eating laundry detergent?

144
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:41,460
我只是想要你告诉我实话
I just need you to tell me the truth.

145
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:42,850
我快被逼疯了
This is driving me crazy.

146
00:06:42,850 --> 00:06:44,750
谢尔顿  他真的会来
Sheldon, he is really coming.

147
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,100
-真的吗  -真的
- Is he?  - He is.

148
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:47,890
-不骗我  -没骗你
- Really? - Yeah.

149
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,930
这下我不知道该相信啥了
Well, now I don't know what to believe!

150
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:55,860
谢谢你带我出来
Thanks for getting me out of the house.

151
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:57,850
我觉得我脑子都快变浆糊了
I feel like my brain is turning to mush.

152
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:59,500
我很乐意帮你
Happy to help.

153
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,700
我有没有给你看孩子们坐着的视频呀
Did I show you the video of the kids sitting?

154
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:05,350
有  你半夜3点发给我了
Yes, you texted it to me at 3:00 a.m.

155
00:07:05,950 --> 00:07:09,020
还以为是谁被抓或者挂了呢
Thought someone was either in jail or dead.

156
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:10,870
抱歉
I'm sorry.

157
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:12,910
没事  至少让我在重新入睡时
No, no, I-it gave me something to watch

158
00:07:12,910 --> 00:07:15,100
有令我想睡的东西看
while I tried to go back to sleep.

159
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:18,140
不行  我不要做那种
You know what? I don't want to be one of those moms

160
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:20,310
只会聊孩子的妈妈
who can only talk about her kids.

161
00:07:20,310 --> 00:07:22,610
好吧  我正在读一本挺有趣的书
Okay, well, I'm reading a pretty good book.

162
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:26,280
关于文艺复兴时期鲜为人知的女艺术家
It's the untold story of female artists during the Renaissance.

163
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,350
我也在读书
Oh, I'm in the middle of a book, too.

164
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:31,280
它有三页长  可以飘在浴缸里
It's three pages long and floats in the bath.

165
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,830
我们也可以聊些其他的
All right, we can talk about something else.

166
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:37,330
你一挤那书  它就呱呱叫
It also quacks when you squeeze it.

167
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:40,440
迈克笑得可开心了  我这儿有视频
You should've seen Michael laugh. I think I have a video.

168
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:43,690
看来没法聊其他的了
Or maybe we can't.

169
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:51,390
好莱坞著名配乐家

170
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:51,390
你的网名怎么叫"约翰·威廉姆斯"
Why is your screen name "John Williams"?

171
00:07:51,570 --> 00:07:55,000
因为哥永远在得分[配乐]
Uh, because I always score.

172
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,860
我要去一趟办公室
Hey, I think I'm gonna head to the office for a little bit.

173
00:07:59,860 --> 00:08:01,310
-周日也去吗  -对呀
- On a Sunday? - Yeah.

174
00:08:01,310 --> 00:08:03,840
我想为明天做好准备
Want to make sure I'm prepared for tomorrow.

175
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:05,440
